Points to be remember:

Install git, ansible, python-pip, jenkins, terraform in the server

pip install boto3

In provider.tf, change the region accordingly

In main.tf, change the AMI ID, Key pair, Subnet-IDs accordingly

In s3.tf, first remove the backend code and change the bucket name. After first build, add again the backend code and change the bucket name.

Create aws_ec2.yml file inside the /opt/ansible/inventory folder

Inside /etc/ansible folder, create Krishav.pem file and give the below permissions
chown jenkins:jenkins Krishav.pem
chmod 400 Krishav.pem

Create the ansible config file by using the below command
ansible-config init --disabled > ansible.cfg

Paste the ansible.cfg data from the github and delete the inventory in line no: 605

Finally deploy the application and run the final check command
ansible -i /opt/ansible/inventory/aws_ec2.yml all -u ec2-user --private-key /etc/ansible/Krishav.pem -m ping

Manual command for deployment:
ansible]# ansible-playbook -i /opt/ansible/inventory/aws_ec2.yml -u ec2-user --private-key=/etc/ansible/Krishav.pem /var/lib/jenkins/workspace/MyDeployment/ansible/deployment.yml
